        {
          "kind": "review",
          "result": "pass",
          "name": "supported finite grammar refutation; universal theorem incomplete.",
          "path": "research/partitions/height-three-unimodality/review-r1.md"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "protocol.json froze the three-primitive tableau grammar before any search. It extends Cho-Huh insertion. At n=7, h=(2,4,4,6,7,7,7), the grammar has an isolated negative state. I re-derived it: M=9 and inv=3. The only incomparable adjacent pair is 6,4, and its reblocking gives invalid rows (2,4) and (6,7). The opposite sector (3,3,1) is empty. This verifies the refutation of a serious frozen method, and the run states its scope correctly. It rules out only that grammar, not a whole class of methods."
    },
